title: Subagent depth limit reached unexpectedly when spawning from main session
updated_at: "2026-08-02T09:36:25Z"
---
When attempting to spawn 4 subagents via the 'subagent' tool from the main session, all failed with 'maximum subagent depth (4) reached'. The main session should be at depth 0 or 1, so hitting depth 4 is unexpected. Need to investigate: (1) whether the session itself counts as a depth level, (2) whether background tasks or context compaction inflate the depth counter, (3) whether the depth is correctly reset between turns after compaction/restart. The session had been compacted and was operating as a non-main session (telegram DM), which may have contributed.